course: dictionary
lesson: 12883
title: A formal word: entirety
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Entirety» is a formal word for all of something, the whole thing. The entirety of a pizza is every slice, from the crust to the last crumb.
explain: You will meet it in exam questions and reports, like «Read the passage in its entirety.» That means read all of it, from start to finish, not just the first paragraph. The clue is «in its» before the word.
explain: To check a meaning, swap in an easy word. «Read the whole passage» means the same as «read the passage in its entirety». If your swap still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
fact: Entirety means all of something, the whole thing.
fact: «In its entirety» means completely, from start to finish.
fact: «The entirety of the class» means every child in the class.
fact: Everyday words that mean about the same are whole and all of.
fact: Entirety is a formal word, so you will see it more in exam questions, reports and stiff speech than in chat.
exercise: «Read the passage in its entirety.» What does in its entirety mean? | Just the first line | Only the parts you like best | *Completely, from start to finish | Quickly, with your eyes shut
exercise: «The entirety of the cake was eaten by the end of the party.» What does entirety mean here? | The plate it sat on | A small slice of the cake | The candles on the cake | *All of the cake
exercise: Which everyday words mean about the same as entirety? | *whole and all of | quick and loud | empty and bare | few and some
test: The teacher said, «Read the story in its entirety before you answer.» What does in its entirety mean? | *From start to finish | Only the last page | Very quickly, skipping lines | Out loud to a friend
test: Which sentence uses entirety correctly? | I ate the entirety of the rain. | The entirety of my pencil is a bird. | *The entirety of the team came to the match, every player. | The entirety is a colour of the sky.
exam: What is the closest meaning to entirety? | piece | corner | edge | *whole
